# Husky hook scripts must keep LF line endings.
# CRLF breaks them under `sh` on Windows (the trailing \r causes
# "command not found" when git invokes the hook).
.husky/* text eol=lf

# Force LF line endings for all text files. CI runs on Linux and GitHub
# Actions' default checkout preserves whatever bytes are in git's object
# store. Files Windows contributors may have committed with CRLF would
# cause byte-for-byte source differences between Windows checkout (CRLF)
# and Linux CI checkout (LF), which breaks sha256-based tests such as
# scoped-id.test.ts (the algorithm hashes the file content; CRLF vs LF
# → different hash on the two platforms). `text=auto` lets git pick text
# vs binary via heuristic; `eol=lf` normalizes text files to LF on the
# next commit that touches them.
* text=auto eol=lf
